  "description": "AGSC-08-20a as amended for 1.1: a commit's actor is the Signed-off-by local part, else the actor that ledger.actors maps the commit's author_email to, else human:unknown. Derivation with ledger.actors = {ada@example.org: human:ada}: (1) the first commit is signed off by bob@example.org although its author is ada@example.org; the sign-off wins, so human:bob; (2) the second has no sign-off and the author ada@example.org, which the map holds, so human:ada; (3) the third has no sign-off and the author eve@example.org, which the map does not hold, so human:unknown; (4) the fourth carries no author_email at all, which is conforming, so human:unknown. The trailing entry is process:agsc. The addresses are used for the look-up only and appear nowhere in the ledger bytes. Without the map the same history gives human:bob, human:unknown, human:unknown, human:unknown, which is the 1.0 result.",
